--- !u!114 &1981225460
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1981225458}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 58fb7818407ae07408994aa0934587f9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: '::'
  checklist: {fileID: 1101813224}
  explanations:
  - afterGroupIndex: 1
    delay: 2
    title: The PC beeps but shows nothing
    why: "The beeping is the computer warning you that it has detected a memory problem
      during startup. The RAM is seated, but its gold contacts are dirty or oxidized,
      so it can\u2019t connect properly to the motherboard."
    howToFix: Put the RAM back into the correct slot. Push it straight down evenly
      until both clips snap into place.
  - afterGroupIndex: 2
    delay: 2
    title: Why turn off the PSU first?
    why: The PSU keeps sending power to the motherboard and everything plugged into
      it even while the computer is shut down, as long as it's still switched on
      and plugged in. Touching or removing parts like RAM while power is still live
      can cause a short circuit, damage the component, or give you a shock. Turning
      the PSU switch off first cuts that power completely, so it's safe to open the
      case and work inside.
    howToFix: 
  - afterGroupIndex: 6
    delay: 2
    title: RAM contacts cleaned
    why: Dirt and oxidation on the gold contacts block the electrical connection
      between the RAM and the slot. Cleaning them restores that connection.
    howToFix: 
