--- !u!114 &2052650475
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2052650473}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 58fb7818407ae07408994aa0934587f9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: '::'
  checklist: {fileID: 1767544737}
  explanations:
  - afterGroupIndex: 1
    delay: 2
    title: The PC shut down by itself
    why: "The computer turned on for a moment, then shut down without showing anything.
      This usually means the RAM is loose or not seated properly. Without working
      memory, the computer can\u2019t finish starting up."
    howToFix: Turn off the PSU switch first for safety. Open the system unit's cover,
      remove the RAM, and push it back firmly into the other slot until the clips
      lock. Then close the cover, turn the PSU back on and press the power button.
  - afterGroupIndex: 2
    delay: 2
    title: Why turn off the PSU first?
    why: The PSU keeps sending power to the motherboard and everything plugged into
      it even while the computer is shut down, as long as it's still switched on
      and plugged in. Touching or removing parts like RAM while power is still live
      can cause a short circuit, damage the component, or give you a shock. Turning
      the PSU switch off first cuts that power completely, so it's safe to open the
      case and work inside.
    howToFix: 
